WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
I'm a co-founder of Salvalo — it's my startup.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.863
Basically, shops close every day with products they

3
00:00:05.863 --> 00:00:08.865
could still sell, and on Salvalo they turn them into

4
00:00:08.865 --> 00:00:11.000
packs with a price and a pickup time.

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.793
Customers find one nearby on the app's map, reserve it,

6
00:00:14.793 --> 00:00:17.759
pay the shop directly and pick it up with a

7
00:00:17.759 --> 00:00:19.000
verification code.

8
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.334
The example I always use: imagine a bakery that has 10

9
00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:25.607
cachitos in the morning, and at 5 in the afternoon it

10
00:00:25.607 --> 00:00:28.200
has 3 left, plus 2 loaves of French bread.

11
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.000
It makes a pack with that.

12
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.113
Of course, to sell it today,

13
00:00:31.113 --> 00:00:34.208
they offer it at a reduced closing price,

14
00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:37.000
and customers go and buy it directly.

15
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.297
The shop wins, because it moves that product instead of

16
00:00:41.297 --> 00:00:44.188
losing it, and it gets more customers

17
00:00:44.188 --> 00:00:47.000
— Salvalo is an extra sales channel.

18
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.376
And the customer gets the same thing:

19
00:00:49.376 --> 00:00:52.780
the same morning cachitos, in the afternoon, on sale,

20
00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.000
super conveniently.

21
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.026
My part: I'm also the technical co-founder

22
00:00:59.026 --> 00:01:03.692
— I redesigned the app and the website;

23
00:01:03.692 --> 00:01:08.000
basically I handle all the frontend.

24
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.409
And I'm also Salvalo's representative here in

25
00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:15.576
Venezuela, so I go out pitching to shops and show up at

26
00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:18.000
every event on Salvalo's behalf.

27
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.098
Honestly, it's pretty great.
